      "id": "httpx-service-client",
      "repo": "httpx",
      "task": "Design a production-style async HTTP client configuration from this repository's documentation. Requirements: a shared AsyncClient rather than one client per request; allow sixty seconds for connection establishment and ten seconds for other timeout operations; at most ten total connections and five idle keep-alive connections with five-second expiry; ignore proxy and certificate environment configuration; opportunistically enable HTTP/2, explain fallback and how to inspect the actual protocol; register an asynchronous response hook that reads the response body before further processing. Explain which failures the transport retry option covers and whether it retries HTTP 503 or read/write failures. Include installation requirements and cleanup. Provide a Python function build_client() returning the configured AsyncClient, the hook, and a short explanation with source citations. Do not send real requests.",
      "checks": [
        "valid timeout object with 60 connect and 10 read/write/pool",
        "limits total10 keepalive5 expiry5",
        "trust_env False",
        "http2 enabled plus dependency/fallback/protocol inspection",
        "async body hook awaits aread",
        "connection-only retry scope",
        "shared client and eventual aclose",
        "source citations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ruff-isolated-ci-config",
      "repo": "ruff",
      "task": "Design a reproducible Ruff CI setup for a project with a root pyproject.toml and conflicting nested config files. Give root configuration selecting E4/E7/E9/F and import sorting, with line length 100 and single-quote formatting. The project requires Python >=3.10; explain target-version inference when no explicit Ruff target is set. Give commands from the root that force this one config for the whole src tree, run lint without modifying code, and check formatting without modifying code. Explain the difference between lint --fix and formatting, whether E501 is automatically enabled by line-length, and the precedence among .ruff.toml, ruff.toml and pyproject.toml in one directory. Cite source sections. Do not execute or edit anything.",
      "checks": [
        "rootselect E4E7E9F I length100 quotesingle",
        "requires-python inference py310",
        "--config pyproject.toml both commands bypass nested",
        "ruff check src nofix",
        "ruff format --check src",
        "lint fixes versus formatting distinction",
        "line-length alone doesnotenable E501",
        ".ruff.toml over ruff.toml over pyproject",
        "citations"
      ]
    }
  ],
